        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t  \n          \n        \n      \n    \n\n    Sat Apr 24, 2027 • 8:00pm\n\n  \n          Comedy\n    \n          Stand Up\n      \n\n\n      Admission $25.00\n    \n      Ticket prices include all taxes and fees.\n    \n  \n\n\n      \n  \n    Buy tickets\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t  \n    \n      \n                  Club Rewind: Brian Patafie\n        \n                  \n            Advance $25 || At the Door $30 ||\nBrian Patafie, known by his fans as \"Comedy’s Original Enter-Trainer\", has quickly become a rising star in North American comedy. Before launching his stand-up career, Brian spent 44 years in the hockey world, working as an athletic trainer in both the NHL, and was the inaugural trainer of the AHL Saint John Flames.  He’s authored two books, Ice It Down and No Days Off, and over the years spent his off-seasons emceeing sports events with a flair for humor. His transition to comedy began in 2021 when he embarked on his No Days Off Tour, honing his skills with writers to craft his unique comedic voice. Since then, Brian’s comedy career has taken off, with sold-out shows across the world.  At seventy years old Brian is ready to embark on his \"ONE LAST TIME\" Tour which brings audiences a mix of hilarious one-liners and a deeply personal, comedic look at his experiences with family, hockey, and life. You don't want to miss the opportunity to see one of professional hockey's most engaging personalities share his hilarious LIFE experiences on stage. \n          \n        \n              \n\n      \n  \n    Event Info\n\n          \n        Category: Comedy      \n    \n          \n        Genre: Stand Up      \n    \n    \n      \n  \n  \t\t\n\n\n      \n      Venue\n\n              Kent Theatre\n      \n              24 Coburg St, Saint John, NB E2L 3J5\n      \n              \n          \n            View on Google Maps\n       